+# Why `com.vk.nightly-review` has never reported anything
+
+Two separate problems. The first hides the second, which is the real failure.
+
+## Cause 1 (fixed): `status` is a read-only variable in zsh
+
+`bin/nightly-review.zsh` line 19 was:
+
+```zsh
+status=$?
+```
+
+In zsh, `status` is a built-in special parameter (an alias for `$?`) and cannot be assigned to. The assignment fails with:
+
+```
+/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status
+```
+
+This is a fatal error in a non-interactive shell, so the script exits with status 1 right there. Everything after line 19 is skipped, including both the failure notice and the success notice. Nothing ever reaches Telegram, and no failure is reported.
+
+This matches the captured state: `last exit code = 1`, and `nightly-review.err` contains the "read-only variable: status" line once per run. I reproduced it with zsh 5.9: the assignment aborts the script with exit 1 before the next line runs.
+
+**Fix:** renamed the variable to `rc` (`rc=$?`, and both uses in the `if` block). I tested the fixed script with a stub `claude` and a stub notifier in a scratch `HOME`:
+- when `claude` fails, it sends `nightly review FAILED (exit 1), see …` and exits 1;
+- when `claude` succeeds, it sends `nightly review done: …` and exits 0.
+
+## Cause 2 (not fixed here): `claude -p` is not logged in under launchd
+
+`nightly-review.err` shows, on every run:
+
+```
+Not logged in · Please run /login
+```
+
+So the headless `claude -p` call fails, which is the real reason the job cannot produce a summary. The job itself runs (launchd finds `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` through the plist's PATH), but the agent has no credentials in that context.
+
+This cannot be fixed from the snapshot, because it depends on your login state. Options:
+- Make sure the same user's login credentials are available to launchd's `gui/501` session. Running `claude` and `/login` interactively as `vk` is the usual first step, then re-run the job by hand with `launchctl kickstart gui/501/com.vk.nightly-review` to check.
+- Or provide an API key to the job by adding `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` under `EnvironmentVariables` in the plist. This stores a secret in a plist, so only do it if you're comfortable with that.
+
+Once Cause 1 is fixed, you will get a `nightly review FAILED (exit 1)` Telegram message each night until Cause 2 is resolved. That is the intended behavior.
+
+## Things I could not verify
+
+- **Telegram token lookup under launchd.** `notify.sh` reads the token with `security find-generic-password -s tg-bot -w`. That works in a normal login session, but I can't check it in the launchd context from the snapshot. The notifier runs with `set -eu`, so if the lookup fails it exits silently. Check by running `launchctl kickstart` after fixing Cause 2, or by running the notifier under `env -i HOME=$HOME PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /bin/zsh -c '~/bin/notify.sh test'`.
+- **Whether `~/bin/nightly-review.zsh` on disk matches the snapshot.** I only changed the snapshot in this folder.
+
+## Applying the fix
+
+Copy the fixed script over the live one. The plist did not change, so no `launchctl` reload is needed; launchd reads the script fresh on each run:
+
+```sh
+cp bin/nightly-review.zsh ~/bin/nightly-review.zsh
+```
